children": [], "description": "Homeostasis identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within biological mechanics across scales. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, homeostasis carries the completed idea into stress, strain, and constitutive laws."}]}, {"id": "eff0c644-4209-4c13-8859-051639ec7b21", "type": "topic", "title": "Stress, strain, and constitutive laws", "description": "This module builds directly on biological mechanics across scales and develops stress, strain, and constitutive laws. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for experimental characterization.", "children": [{"id": "4c83c99d-c2be-44a2-9213-b55d181d65b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tensors conceptually", "children": [], "description": "Tensors conceptually identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within stress, strain, and constitutive laws. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before elasticity because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "5515fddb-02cf-47d3-af09-c2c1798082a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Elasticity", "children": [], "description": "Elasticity identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within stress, strain, and constitutive laws. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After tensors conceptually, elasticity supplies what is needed to address viscoelasticity."}, {"id": "5c30ee94-40e6-4350-a4bd-00557047ca99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Viscoelasticity", "children": [], "description": "Viscoelasticity identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within stress, strain, and constitutive laws. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, viscoelasticity carries the completed idea into experimental characterization."}]}, {"id": "9fe75062-72a3-42b3-b5b5-c72aab5393a7", "type": "topic", "title": "Experimental characterization", "description": "This module builds directly on stress, strain, and constitutive laws and develops experimental characterization. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for bone and connective tissue.", "children": [{"id": "d53b03db-dbfb-4fb4-b888-d87e0d4ccb52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Uniaxial tests", "children": [], "description": "Uniaxial tests identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within experimental characterization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before creep because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "2d506950-b379-483a-ac10-04a18fdeb215", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creep", "children": [], "description": "Creep identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within experimental characterization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After uniaxial tests, creep supplies what is needed to address relaxation."}, {"id": "7bc408e3-ba44-43b6-93d2-dd9f9563db5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relaxation", "children": [], "description": "Relaxation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within experimental characterization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After creep, relaxation supplies what is needed to address parameter fitting."}, {"id": "4f6c5801-8307-4400-b9ab-0a81f540a306", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Parameter fitting", "children": [], "description": "Parameter fitting identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within experimental characterization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, parameter fitting carries the completed idea into bone and connective tissue."}]}, {"id": "d00c1e9d-f451-4909-a43c-d0a4d5267b25", "type": "topic", "title": "Bone and connective tissue", "description": "This module builds directly on experimental characterization and develops bone and connective tissue. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for muscle mechanics.", "children": [{"id": "e42202a8-7682-44b7-87db-11503b1c2dca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anisotropy", "children": [], "description": "Anisotropy identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within bone and connective tissue. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before remodeling because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "40bc64f2-e94d-4c85-bfeb-46bd904fd3ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Remodeling", "children": [], "description": "Remodeling gives bone and connective tissue a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. After anisotropy, remodeling supplies what is needed to address fracture."}, {"id": "50766749-9953-4eeb-91b4-d941edb89cdd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fracture", "children": [], "description": "Fracture identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within bone and connective tissue. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After remodeling, fracture supplies what is needed to address structure–function."}, {"id": "6890bb1c-7592-4c96-a624-cdf1a97870ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structure–function", "children": [], "description": "Structure–function identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within bone and connective tissue. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, structure–function carries the completed idea into muscle mechanics."}]}, {"id": "386aaf87-bbd3-4e82-a87c-78e786387539", "type": "topic", "title": "Muscle mechanics", "description": "This module builds directly on bone and connective tissue and develops muscle mechanics. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for joint and limb statics.", "children": [{"id": "3940088e-dacd-4969-9e9d-c5468f885609", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Force–length", "children": [], "description": "Force–length is a governing quantity in muscle mechanics, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. It appears before force–velocity because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "5e85d3de-8f46-453b-b940-75759f9ec208", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Force–velocity", "children": [], "description": "Force–velocity is a governing quantity in muscle mechanics, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. After force–length, force–velocity supplies what is needed to address activation."}, {"id": "5a6ac43e-f405-47c3-800b-7ceab17ef8ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Activation", "children": [], "description": "Activation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within muscle mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After force–velocity, activation supplies what is needed to address hill-type models."}, {"id": "37a85cd5-889d-4922-8cc3-6f0ea077a912", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hill-type models", "children": [], "description": "Hill-type models gives muscle mechanics a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, hill-type models carries the completed idea into joint and limb statics."}]}, {"id": "21123736-8932-4c40-9375-52f0462d713a", "type": "topic", "title": "Joint and limb statics", "description": "This module builds directly on muscle mechanics and develops joint and limb statics. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for motion and gait.", "children": [{"id": "2ccdef5e-7254-47cc-bda7-f78108023937", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moment arms", "children": [], "description": "Moment arms identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within joint and limb statics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before inverse dynamics because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "e0753ca8-b0bf-425e-8f06-120c09278c00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inverse dynamics", "children": [], "description": "Inverse dynamics identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within joint and limb statics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After moment arms, inverse dynamics supplies what is needed to address load sharing."}, {"id": "5cd35600-2ab2-4e69-a8aa-729f6ff62620", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Load sharing", "children": [], "description": "Load sharing identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within joint and limb statics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, load sharing carries the completed idea into motion and gait."}]}, {"id": "63696f2f-7287-4500-8f73-fd2da1c31650", "type": "topic", "title": "Motion and gait", "description": "This module builds directly on joint and limb statics and develops motion and gait. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for cardiovascular fluid mechanics.", "children": [{"id": "95cceb62-85e8-4024-a3bd-98d31a65233b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kinematics", "children": [], "description": "Kinematics identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within motion and gait. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before kinetics because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "654cd8a9-de2c-4327-9b45-e2e3d48ba6a3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kinetics", "children": [], "description": "Kinetics identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within motion and gait. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After kinematics, kinetics supplies what is needed to address ground reaction forces."}, {"id": "bef5097c-0702-4333-98ee-a0cd108a57c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ground reaction forces", "children": [], "description": "Ground reaction forces supplies the causal sequence within motion and gait, which is necessary for predicting unfamiliar outcomes instead of memorizing examples. After kinetics, ground reaction forces supplies what is needed to address work and power."}, {"id": "c1213a0e-27ac-4295-88e7-2c52bb2f10a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Work and power", "children": [], "description": "Work and power identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within motion and gait. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, work and power carries the completed idea into cardiovascular fluid mechanics."}]}, {"id": "d5918759-cbce-4664-b734-61c646444b1d", "type": "topic", "title": "Cardiovascular fluid mechanics", "description": "This module builds directly on motion and gait and develops cardiovascular fluid mechanics. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for respiratory mechanics.", "children": [{"id": "5e5b0758-b937-41a4-89f8-304487d3f990", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pressure/flow", "children": [], "description": "Pressure/flow identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cardiovascular fluid mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before poiseuille because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "5ee43446-fed8-44e6-9b13-0d6f8bb464d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poiseuille", "children": [], "description": "Poiseuille identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cardiovascular fluid mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After pressure/flow, poiseuille supplies what is needed to address pulsatility."}, {"id": "ac0a1b63-07d1-4258-92ba-7f9422f4c079", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pulsatility", "children": [], "description": "Pulsatility identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cardiovascular fluid mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After poiseuille, pulsatility supplies what is needed to address compliance."}, {"id": "18ed3b6d-4f9c-402d-a642-1452eab717b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compliance", "children": [], "description": "Compliance identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cardiovascular fluid mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, compliance carries the completed idea into respiratory mechanics."}]}, {"id": "8b5687e7-c8a8-46fe-9676-b9b2e3c44e8a", "type": "topic", "title": "Respiratory mechanics", "description": "This module builds directly on cardiovascular fluid mechanics and develops respiratory mechanics. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for cell and membrane mechanics.", "children": [{"id": "cf9022d8-8f92-41c9-80aa-dbbcc2c43bef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Airway resistance", "children": [], "description": "Airway resistance identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within respiratory mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before lung compliance because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "d486305f-4a8c-4567-864f-8c6eb76beed4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lung compliance", "children": [], "description": "Lung compliance identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within respiratory mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After airway resistance, lung compliance supplies what is needed to address work of breathing."}, {"id": "b8c5c66a-c2fd-4288-965c-3f6b4a209ff3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Work of breathing", "children": [], "description": "Work of breathing identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within respiratory mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, work of breathing carries the completed idea into cell and membrane mechanics."}]}, {"id": "6d4034c7-c21a-4834-b190-42d5269e4e36", "type": "topic", "title": "Cell and membrane mechanics", "description": "This module builds directly on respiratory mechanics and develops cell and membrane mechanics. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for transport in tissues.", "children": [{"id": "053de934-2b2a-48f0-ba9a-492f446506de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cytoskeleton", "children": [], "description": "Cytoskeleton identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cell and membrane mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before adhesion because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "0e95e843-2bf3-4049-956b-c5fa66a83aa6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adhesion", "children": [], "description": "Adhesion identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cell and membrane mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After cytoskeleton, adhesion supplies what is needed to address membrane tension."}, {"id": "4982df0f-bc9c-4a6a-844d-df1b24e18a62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Membrane tension", "children": [], "description": "Membrane tension identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cell and membrane mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After adhesion, membrane tension supplies what is needed to address mechanotransduction."}, {"id": "2c63fb5e-757d-4ffa-b3a3-639cb6dd44cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mechanotransduction", "children": [], "description": "Mechanotransduction identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cell and membrane mechanics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, mechanotransduction carries the completed idea into transport in tissues."}]}, {"id": "019710cc-c49e-423c-947c-498eb7195537", "type": "topic", "title": "Transport in tissues", "description": "This module builds directly on cell and membrane mechanics and develops transport in tissues. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for mechanobiology and design.", "children": [{"id": "589a5a3f-40e9-4fb3-bf8a-49dcf4ab6161", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diffusion", "children": [], "description": "Diffusion identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within transport in tissues. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before convection because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "1612b22c-4929-4eb3-ad2d-fe8acb4ee606", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Convection", "children": [], "description": "Convection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within transport in tissues. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After diffusion, convection supplies what is needed to address poroelasticity."}, {"id": "5b5afae6-4c3b-4c7a-8168-c4d1d1263c1e", "type": "subtopic", 