": "Implants", "children": [], "description": "Implants identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mechanobiology and design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After injury, implants supplies what is needed to address validation."}, {"id": "9c9d3f58-49bf-45f9-bf03-77824342f786", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Validation", "children": [], "description": "Validation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mechanobiology and design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After implants, validation supplies what is needed to address ethical model use."}, {"id": "00b38111-7abb-4766-bebb-26664e2daa52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical model use", "children": [], "description": "Ethical model use gives mechanobiology and design a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final course topic, ethical model use requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$biomechzzjs$::jsonb,
